  (text "kisi 0.3.3: lane BUS_P – linear test bench\nEach element symbol calls its subcircuit in BUS_P.lib through a wrapper `<name>_k` in BUS_P_kicad.lib (reference node = ground).\nA part's Value is its subcircuit parameter c, r or l (Sim.Params refers to the Value field; SPICE notation): edit the value, the parasitics stay.\nProbe the receiver die; for a pair the difference of P and N. Inspect → Simulator → Run.\nAdd a termination or swap the ends here; IBIS ends: replace the source/receiver by KiCad IBIS symbols." (at 38.10 38.10 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid daae3ccd-e9b6-4a0c-8347-259134c2422a)
  )
  (text ".tran 3.000000e-11 2.566306e-7" (at 38.10 45.72 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid fef351e0-5ef1-4c31-8108-1078af7612b1)
  )
  (text "Transmitter (per line, P and N in opposite phase): profile lvds, 1.000 Gbit/s, PRBS7, edge 300.0 ps (10-90 %).\nThevenin source: emf ±14.76 V behind R 5000 Ω, C 2.000 pF at the die.\nR ≫ the receiver's 60.00 Ω: a current-mode driver as its Thevenin equivalent, I = emf/(R + 60.00 Ω) = 2.917 mA per line.\nThe emf is scaled so that the receiver sees ±0.3500 V at DC differential.\n\nReceiver (per line): R 60.00 Ω and C 2.000 pF from the die to ground.\nA 120.0 Ω differential termination, split into two halves to the reference.\nProbe the die nodes (top of CRX/RRX): V(P) − V(N).\nNote: termination R1 at U2 used as the receiver termination (60 Ω per line)" (at 38.10 132.08 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 1b9725be-d450-4e36-8ff4-01c81cc39271)
  )
